# These feed the frozen scorer and define the holdout / hierarchy / weights, so they
# are as security-critical as the scorer itself. Freezing them closes the gap where an
# agent could change the scored number without touching a "frozen" file:
#   scoring.py     — assembles the sales/calendar/prices frames the frozen scorer sees
#   data.py        — loader + verify_manifest (snapshot integrity gate)
#   contract.py    — validate(): the structural no-target-columns / full-grid check
#   adapters/m5.py — holdout cut, manifest, 12-level hierarchy, dollar-weight inputs
/src/scoring.py    @rslayer
/src/data.py       @rslayer
/src/contract.py   @rslayer
/src/adapters/m5.py @rslayer

/tools/make_fixture.py @rslayer
